# A backslash written as `\u{5c}` is text and escapes nothing after it: the
# interpolation after it still interpolates, and the quote after it still
# closes the String. Subtle: `\\` and `\u{5c}` yield the same character, but
# escapes decode once, never forming new ones.
#= {result: ['\\7', '\\', '\\$7'], inputs: {x: 7}}
[$'\u{5c}${x}', $'\u{5c}', $'\u{5c}$${x}']
